# PROJECT: NearMart 3D — Interactive Virtual Supermarket & Local Grocery Marketplace

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, 3D web developer, UI/UX designer, and database architect.

Build a complete, modern, responsive, full-stack web application named **NearMart 3D**. This is a college final-year project designed to transform traditional grocery shopping into an interactive virtual supermarket experience while connecting customers with nearby physical supermarkets.

The website must work on desktop, laptop, tablet, and mobile browsers.

Do not build only a static landing page or a UI prototype. Build a functional application with frontend, backend APIs, database integration, authentication, shopping cart, inventory management, order processing, and an interactive 3D supermarket.

If a feature requires external credentials or a paid service, provide a working demo mode and clearly document how to configure the real integration.

# 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Create a platform where customers can:

1. Register and log in.
2. Discover supermarkets near their location.
3. Select a supermarket and view its available products.
4. Enter an interactive 3D virtual supermarket.
5. Walk through aisles and explore product shelves.
6. Click products to view details, prices, images, and availability.
7. Add products to their shopping cart.
8. Place grocery orders from a selected supermarket.
9. Choose home delivery or pickup when supported.
10. Track order status.
11. View their order history.

Supermarket owners must be able to manage their stores, products, prices, stock quantities, and customer orders.

Administrators must be able to manage customers, supermarkets, products, and platform activity.

